# 基础词 Unit03
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 基础词Unit03核心词汇

{{ancient}}{{/ˈeɪnʃənt}}{{adj. 古代的；古老的}}{{The ancient temple has stood for over two thousand years.}}
{{anger}}{{/ˈæŋɡər}}{{n./v. 愤怒；使发怒}}{{He tried to control his anger during the argument.}}
{{angle}}{{/ˈæŋɡl}}{{n. 角度；视角}}{{Let's look at the problem from a different angle.}}
{{angry}}{{/ˈæŋɡri}}{{adj. 生气的；愤怒的}}{{She was angry about the unfair treatment.}}
{{animal}}{{/ˈænɪml}}{{n. 动物}}{{Many animal species are facing extinction.}}
{{anniversary}}{{/ˌænɪˈvɜːsəri}}{{n. 周年纪念日}}{{They celebrated their wedding anniversary with a dinner party.}}
{{announce}}{{/əˈnaʊns}}{{v. 宣布；通知}}{{The company announced a new product launch.}}
{{annual}}{{/ˈænjuəl}}{{adj. 年度的；每年的}}{{The annual report shows significant growth in revenue.}}
{{anonymous}}{{/əˈnɒnɪməs}}{{adj. 匿名的；无名的}}{{The donation was made by an anonymous donor.}}
{{another}}{{/əˈnʌðər}}{{adj./pron. 另一个；又一个}}{{Would you like another cup of coffee?}}
{{answer}}{{/ˈɑːnsər}}{{n./v. 回答；答案}}{{She gave a clear and concise answer to the question.}}
{{anxiety}}{{/æŋˈzaɪəti}}{{n. 焦虑；不安}}{{Exam anxiety is a common problem among students.}}
{{anxious}}{{/ˈæŋkʃəs}}{{adj. 焦虑的；渴望的}}{{He felt anxious about the job interview.}}
{{any}}{{/ˈeni}}{{adj./pron. 任何；一些}}{{Is there any water left in the bottle?}}
{{anyhow}}{{/ˈenihaʊ}}{{adv. 无论如何；不管怎样}}{{Anyhow, we should try our best to finish on time.}}
{{anyway}}{{/ˈeniweɪ}}{{adv. 无论如何；总之}}{{It was raining, but we went hiking anyway.}}
{{apart}}{{/əˈpɑːt}}{{adv. 分开地；相距地}}{{The two cities are 200 kilometers apart.}}
{{apartment}}{{/əˈpɑːtmənt}}{{n. 公寓}}{{They rented a small apartment near the university.}}
{{apologize}}{{/əˈpɒlədʒaɪz}}{{v. 道歉}}{{He apologized for being late to the meeting.}}
{{apparent}}{{/əˈpærənt}}{{adj. 明显的；表面上的}}{{It was apparent that she was not telling the truth.}}
{{appeal}}{{/əˈpiːl}}{{v./n. 呼吁；上诉；吸引力}}{{The charity made an appeal for donations.}}
{{appear}}{{/əˈpɪər}}{{v. 出现；似乎}}{{The sun appeared from behind the clouds.}}
{{appetite}}{{/ˈæpɪtaɪt}}{{n. 食欲；胃口}}{{The long walk gave me a good appetite.}}
{{apple}}{{/ˈæpl}}{{n. 苹果}}{{An apple a day keeps the doctor away.}}
{{apply}}{{/əˈplaɪ}}{{v. 申请；应用；适用}}{{She applied for a scholarship to study abroad.}}
{{appoint}}{{/əˈpɔɪnt}}{{v. 任命；指定}}{{He was appointed as the new department manager.}}
{{appreciate}}{{/əˈpriːʃieɪt}}{{v. 感激；欣赏}}{{I really appreciate your help with this project.}}
{{approach}}{{/əˈprəʊtʃ}}{{v./n. 接近；方法}}{{We need to approach this problem from a different perspective.}}
{{appropriate}}{{/əˈprəʊpriət}}{{adj. 适当的；合适的}}{{Please wear appropriate clothing for the interview.}}
{{approve}}{{/əˈpruːv}}{{v. 批准；赞成}}{{The board approved the new budget plan.}}
{{approximate}}{{/əˈprɒksɪmət}}{{adj./v. 大约的；接近}}{{The approximate cost of the project is one million dollars.}}
{{architect}}{{/ˈɑːkɪtekt}}{{n. 建筑师；设计师}}{{The architect designed a modern and eco-friendly building.}}
{{area}}{{/ˈeəriə}}{{n. 地区；领域；面积}}{{This area is known for its beautiful scenery.}}
{{argue}}{{/ˈɑːɡjuː}}{{v. 争论；主张}}{{They argued about the best way to solve the problem.}}
{{arise}}{{/əˈraɪz}}{{v. 出现；产生}}{{New challenges may arise during the project.}}
{{army}}{{/ˈɑːmi}}{{n. 军队；陆军}}{{The army was deployed to assist in the disaster relief.}}
{{around}}{{/əˈraʊnd}}{{prep./adv. 围绕；大约}}{{The earth revolves around the sun.}}
{{arrange}}{{/əˈreɪndʒ}}{{v. 安排；整理}}{{She arranged the flowers in a beautiful vase.}}
{{arrest}}{{/əˈrest}}{{v./n. 逮捕；阻止}}{{The police arrested the suspect last night.}}
{{arrival}}{{/əˈraɪvl}}{{n. 到达；抵达}}{{Upon arrival at the airport, we went straight to the hotel.}}
{{artificial}}{{/ˌɑːtɪˈfɪʃl}}{{adj. 人工的；人造的}}{{Artificial intelligence is transforming many industries.}}
{{aside}}{{/əˈsaɪd}}{{adv. 在旁边；到旁边}}{{She stepped aside to let the others pass.}}
{{aspect}}{{/ˈæspekt}}{{n. 方面；层面}}{{We need to consider every aspect of the problem.}}
{{assemble}}{{/əˈsembl}}{{v. 集合；组装}}{{The students assembled in the auditorium for the lecture.}}
{{assess}}{{/əˈses}}{{v. 评估；评价}}{{Teachers assess students' progress through regular tests.}}
{{asset}}{{/ˈæset}}{{n. 资产；有价值的人或物}}{{Her experience is a valuable asset to the company.}}
{{assign}}{{/əˈsaɪn}}{{v. 分配；指定}}{{The teacher assigned homework to the students.}}
{{assist}}{{/əˈsɪst}}{{v. 帮助；协助}}{{The nurse assisted the doctor during the operation.}}
{{associate}}{{/əˈsəʊʃieɪt}}{{v./n. 联系；同事}}{{People often associate the color red with passion.}}
{{assume}}{{/əˈsjuːm}}{{v. 假设；承担}}{{Let's assume that the project will be completed on time.}}
{{assure}}{{/əˈʃʊər}}{{v. 保证；使确信}}{{I assure you that the product is of high quality.}}
{{atmosphere}}{{/ˈætməsfɪər}}{{n. 大气；气氛}}{{The restaurant has a warm and friendly atmosphere.}}
{{attach}}{{/əˈtætʃ}}{{v. 附上；重视}}{{Please attach your resume to the email.}}
{{attack}}{{/əˈtæk}}{{v./n. 攻击；发作}}{{The army launched a surprise attack at dawn.}}
{{attain}}{{/əˈteɪn}}{{v. 达到；获得}}{{She attained the highest score in the class.}}
{{attempt}}{{/əˈtempt}}{{v./n. 尝试；企图}}{{He attempted to climb the mountain but failed.}}
{{attend}}{{/əˈtend}}{{v. 出席；照料}}{{All students are expected to attend the lecture.}}
{{attention}}{{/əˈtenʃn}}{{n. 注意；关注}}{{Please pay attention to the safety instructions.}}
{{attitude}}{{/ˈætɪtjuːd}}{{n. 态度；看法}}{{A positive attitude is essential for success.}}
{{attract}}{{/əˈtrækt}}{{v. 吸引；引起}}{{The exhibition attracted thousands of visitors.}}
{{audience}}{{/ˈɔːdiəns}}{{n. 观众；听众}}{{The audience applauded enthusiastically after the performance.}}
{{authority}}{{/ɔːˈθɒrəti}}{{n. 权威；当局}}{{The local authority approved the construction plan.}}
{{automatic}}{{/ˌɔːtəˈmætɪk}}{{adj. 自动的；无意识的}}{{The door has an automatic locking system.}}
{{available}}{{/əˈveɪləbl}}{{adj. 可用的；有空的}}{{The manager is not available at the moment.}}
{{average}}{{/ˈævərɪdʒ}}{{n./adj. 平均；一般的}}{{The average temperature in summer is 30 degrees.}}
{{avoid}}{{/əˈvɔɪd}}{{v. 避免；避开}}{{You should avoid eating too much sugar.}}
{{awake}}{{/əˈweɪk}}{{adj./v. 醒着的；唤醒}}{{I was awake all night worrying about the exam.}}
{{award}}{{/əˈwɔːd}}{{n./v. 奖；授予}}{{She received an award for her outstanding research.}}
{{aware}}{{/əˈweər}}{{adj. 意识到的；知道的}}{{Are you aware of the risks involved in this project?}}
{{awful}}{{/ˈɔːfl}}{{adj. 可怕的；糟糕的}}{{The weather was awful during our vacation.}}
